<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="energy_market_stress::diesel_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Physical interruptions to production, pipelines or loading terminals reduce available diesel volumes on markets, raising spot prices through tighter immediate supply.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_market_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_bond_shock::long_term_nominal_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute interruptions to Russian energy flows raise near-term inflation expectations and term premia as markets price higher future policy rates and energy-related sovereign risk, lifting long-dated nominal yields globally.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="iran_regional_conflict::military_escalation" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Disruptions to global energy supply from the Russia-Ukraine war elevate fuel and shipping security concerns, prompting states and non-state actors in the Middle East to increase naval escorts, interdiction missions and pre-emptive strikes to secure routes and facilities, raising regional kinetic intensity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="us_china_rivalry::bilat_political_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">War-driven disruptions in European and global energy markets push China to deepen energy and strategic ties with Russia (e.g., increased imports, long‑term contracts), which the United States interprets as geopolitical alignment and responds with diplomatic pressure and strategic countermeasures that raise bilateral tensions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
