<edge source="us_china_rivalry::tech_decouple_degree" target="global_bond_shock::long_term_nominal_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater technological decoupling fragments global R&amp;D and supply chains, lowering long-run productivity and expected real growth and thereby reducing equilibrium real rates and pressuring long-term nominal sovereign yields downward.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::tech_decouple_degree" target="iran_regional_conflict::proxy_attack_frequency" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Deeper technological decoupling incentivizes alternative bilateral tech and dual‑use transfers outside established multinational controls (including from actors seeking to hedge ties with the US), enhancing Iranian and proxy strike capabilities and raising the rate of proxy attacks over time.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
