<edge source="us_china_rivalry::export_control_strength" target="energy_market_stress::refiner_run_rates" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls on specialized refinery equipment, catalysts and control software impede timely procurement and maintenance of critical components, forcing some refineries to cut throughput or run at lower utilization.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_market_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::export_control_strength" target="global_bond_shock::corporate_funding_cost" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls on sensitive components and dual-use goods directly depress affected firms' revenues and raise perceived default and operational risk, widening credit spreads and raising corporate borrowing costs for those issuers and related sectors.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::export_control_strength" target="iran_regional_conflict::sanctions_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter US export controls prompt enforcement responses and broadened use of secondary measures (targeting intermediaries and technology channels), which leads to more frequent and severe sanctions actions related to Iran to prevent evasion.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
