<edge source="global_bond_shock::fiscal_fin_pressure" target="energy_market_stress::policy_export_restrictio" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased fiscal financing pressure raises the political and budgetary incentive for governments to restrict diesel exports to protect domestic supply, limit subsidy burdens, or suppress local price inflation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_market_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::fiscal_fin_pressure" target="iran_regional_conflict::proxy_attack_frequency" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher sovereign financing stress in Gulf backers forces near-term budget cuts and delays to off‑budget transfers, directly reducing cash flows to allied militias and lowering the rate of proxy strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::fiscal_fin_pressure" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising sovereign financing stress in major sanctioning states raises the political and budgetary cost of maintaining broad, long-duration sanctions and enforcement programs, reducing the scope or intensity of sanctions they apply to Russia.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::fiscal_fin_pressure" target="us_china_rivalry::trade_barrier_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising fiscal financing pressure pushes governments to protect domestic industry and revenue streams through tariffs, quotas or conditional subsidies, increasing the intensity of trade barriers affecting bilateral commerce.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
