  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher diesel export volumes increase export receipts and tax/royalty revenues for the sovereign, reducing immediate financing needs and lowering market-implied fiscal financing pressure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_stress::diesel_export_volume" target="iran_regional_conflict::diplomatic_engagement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden drop in diesel exports creates acute supply shortfalls for import-dependent states and commercial actors, prompting rapid bilateral and multilateral diplomatic negotiations, emergency talks, and requests for exemptions or alternative supplies.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_stress::diesel_export_volume" target="iran_regional_conflict::proxy_attack_frequency" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Lower diesel export volumes reduce a direct source of revenue and in-kind fuel transfers that have been used to finance and sustain Iran's proxy networks, leading to a measurable decline in their strike frequency as resources tighten.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_stress::diesel_export_volume" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
