  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp, sustained diesel price spikes raise transport and manufacturing costs and domestic inflation, triggering politically driven protectionist measures (tariffs, quotas, emergency import controls) by both Washington and Beijing to shield industries, increasing trade barrier intensity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
